/* book Worked example 2: Q: A three-channel Holter samples each channel at 250 samples per second and stores each 12-bit sample in 1.5 bytes. How much memory does a 24-hour record need, and how many such records fit on a 1 GB card?
   1. Recording time = 24 × 3600 = 86,400 s.
   2. Samples per channel = 250 × 86,400 = 21.6 × 10⁶.
   3. All three channels = 3 × 21.6 × 10⁶ = 64.8 × 10⁶ samples.
   4. Memory = 64.8 × 10⁶ × 1.5 bytes = 97.2 × 10⁶ bytes = 97.2 MB.
   5. Records on 1 GB = 10⁹ ÷ 97.2 × 10⁶ = 10.3, so ten full days.
   Answer: A 24-hour three-channel record needs 97.2 MB, so a 1 GB card holds about ten days of recording. */
